1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,960
You can even win a reward!

2
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:08,560
I adjusted the transfer circle.

3
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:12,697
Now it will only facilitate travel between
here and the Clearflow Lake Stratum.

4
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:14,797
Oh, and don't worry,
monsters can't use it.

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,220
I made sure. Yay!

6
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,437
Good work, Hulemy!

7
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:18,402
Yes, well done.

8
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,917
Oh, working hard, huh?

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,529
Gotta say, I am impressed.

10
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:26,857
Once things settle down a bit, we should
head to the Clearflow Lake Stratum.

11
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:28,797
Hey, we're done with our patrol duty.

12
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:31,292
I didn't see any remnants in the village.

13
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,600
Man, I'm tired.

14
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:37,280
Captain, wanna tell me why I got
paired with the pervert? Who? Where?

15
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:39,932
Is someone using illusion magic, perhaps?

16
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,554
Where is the pervert of whom you speak?

17
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:45,637
Each of us has to take
their turn standing watch.

18
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:47,417
That's just the way it worked out.

19
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,147
Oh, I take no issue with it.

20
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:53,656
After all, is it not a gentleman's
duty to protect a small, frail lady?

21
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:56,640
Hey, Shui, relax!

22
00:00:56,780 --> 00:00:57,837
Don't tell me to relax!

23
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:00,377
He kept digging old shoes
out of the collapsed houses,

24
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:02,837
and I had to watch his nose twitch
while he tried to smell them.

25
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:03,861
It's disgusting!

26
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,230
How sad.

27
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:07,897
I did not know she was emotionally
unstable, the poor dear.

28
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:09,720
Snip this! Get at it!

29
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:13,916
Well, this is some high-level combat.

30
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:16,395
Too bad it's between comrades, though.

31
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:19,800
Hey, Boxxo, you got a
moment to talk? Yeah.

32
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:21,680
I appreciate it.

33
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:25,557
Do you think you could stop by the Menagerie
of Fool's base once you're done here?

34
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:26,720
Eh? Here?

35
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,471
Yeah, in the origin stratum, conveniently.

36
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:42,624
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul.

37
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:43,897
In this new world of wonders,

38
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:46,897
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super-strong partner,

39
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:47,810
Lamas.

40
00:01:47,893 --> 00:01:49,900
The name's Boxo. Hello there.

41
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:51,880
That means yes, by the way.

42
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,150
Interesting.

43
00:03:08,233 --> 00:03:11,781
I didn't know the Menagerie had
their base in the Origins, Stratum.

44
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:14,377
Thanks for agreeing to talk, my friends.

45
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:18,342
We have something we need to tell
you, and it's long past overdue.

46
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:20,837
Yes, it is.

47
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:22,237
They deserve to know.

48
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,340
It'd be best.

49
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:24,890
Hold on.

50
00:03:24,973 --> 00:03:27,277
Did I just see a shadow
cross Vilmina's face?

51
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:30,517
The red and white twins' mood
seems to have shifted, too.

52
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,060
What is going on here?

53
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:35,017
Come on, that's enough
messing around, you two!

54
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:36,677
Just give me a few more minutes!

55
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:39,257
I almost sunk one right
through this jerk's eye!

56
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:40,170
This is odd.

57
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:42,277
Is someone using mental
manipulation magic?

58
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:44,713
Because I hear strange childish chatter.

59
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:46,370
Sorry.

60
00:03:46,453 --> 00:03:49,057
Seems we'll have to wait for
these two fools to settle down.

61
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,377
But then you can all
follow us to our base.

62
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:52,290
Hello there!

63
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:55,280
This is all news to me.

64
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:59,077
I had no idea the Menagerie of Fools
base was in the Origin Stratum.

65
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,397
Yeah, we didn't want many people to know.

66
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:04,997
Hey, how long have you been a member
of the Menagerie of Fools, Shui?

67
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:07,000
Hasn't even been two years yet.

68
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:10,737
Wait, are you telling me that Heavy's
been a member longer than you have?

69
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:12,840
Yes, I am indeed her senior.

70
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:15,497
Though it is worth noting
that we do not operate under a

71
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:18,977
troublesome vertical hierarchy
here in the Menagerie of Fools.

72
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:19,890
If we did,

73
00:04:19,973 --> 00:04:24,237
that would require me to treat Aka and
Shiro with the respect one shows a superior.

74
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:25,160
I'm confused.

75
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:27,477
Aren't the twins quite
a bit younger than you?

76
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:28,972
You are correct, Hulemy.

77
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,110
Nevertheless,

78
00:04:30,193 --> 00:04:34,297
the founding members of the menagerie are
Captain Kerioyl, Vice-Captain Filmina,

79
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,300
and then Aka and Shiro as well.

80
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,780
Those four started it all. Oh really?

81
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:41,117
I didn't even know that
and I'm a member too.

82
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,057
It's the first time Shui's heard this too?

83
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:46,697
Now that you mention it, those four
all disappear at once pretty often,

84
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:48,797
and they seem to work together a lot.

85
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:52,056
If you're curious, you should
ask them about it later.

86
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:53,290
What?

87
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,360
Oh, forgive my inattention, Master Boxo.

88
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,477
Hearing all that reminded me,

89
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:01,357
there's something I've been wondering
about for quite a while now.

90
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,270
Yes!

91
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:05,457
It's a sense I have about
Aka and Shiro's presence.

92
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:06,560
No, never mind.

93
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:10,299
I shouldn't go around
speculating about such things.

94
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:14,345
Well, now that you said something,
I am going to fixate on that.

95
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:17,877
What is...

96
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:20,600
Here you have it, the Menagerie's base.

97
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:23,757
Well, there's plenty of
ventilation, I'll give you that.

98
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,260
Oh, that's a decoy.

99
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:28,680
The real base is beyond this hidden door.

100
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:34,100
All right, come on down, everyone.

101
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,500
Hey, please, wherever you'd like, friends.

102
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:42,577
Boxo, would you mind dispensing
some refreshments for everyone?

103
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:43,490
Hello there!

104
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:47,980
Welcome to the Menagerie of Fools hideout.

105
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,837
We've gathered you here
today for one reason.

106
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:54,273
We figured it's time to share
our objective with you all.

107
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:56,980
First, a quick review.

108
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,257
I'm sure you all remember
how you can have a single

109
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:01,797
wish granted if you're able
to master this dungeon,

110
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:02,710
right?

111
00:06:02,793 --> 00:06:04,557
I shall grant thee one
wish of thy choosing!

112
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:07,257
But only if thou reachest
the lowest stratum?

113
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:09,877
And offerest thy proof
that thou hast subdued.

114
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:12,240
a formidable stratum lord, end quote.

115
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:13,618
So goes the legend.

116
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:16,137
Yeah, and there was once a team?

117
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:17,937
Who reached the bottom
stratum of a dungeon!

118
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:19,608
in a land to the southwest.

119
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:23,457
Word in the strata is that they
did get their wishes granted.

120
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:27,220
But that's apparently when the
dungeon ceased to exist. What?

121
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:28,297
That means...

122
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:30,597
Are you saying that if somebody
gets their wish granted,

123
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:33,017
the Clearflow Lake stratum
will just disappear?

124
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,557
That's what I'm getting at.

125
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:38,637
And what happens to all the people
inside a dungeon when it ceases to exist?

126
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:42,157
Well, as I understand, they
get forcefully ejected from it.

127
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,070
But don't worry,

128
00:06:43,153 --> 00:06:47,452
I made good and sure that nobody would
be destroyed along with the dungeon.

129
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:48,730
Good.

130
00:06:48,813 --> 00:06:50,817
So the residents won't
get caught up in it.

131
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:51,730
So yeah.

132
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:56,397
The Vice-Captain and I felt it was
time that we revealed our wish.

133
00:06:56,480 --> 00:07:00,421
And we're sorry to have kept it a
secret from you for so damn long.

134
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:05,470
What?

135
00:07:05,553 --> 00:07:08,157
There's actually been a
door there this whole time?

136
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,440
Follow me this way.

137
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:15,690
Huh?

138
00:07:15,773 --> 00:07:17,400
What in the world is that?

139
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,802
Seriously, what's going on here?

140
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:25,457
While it is faint, I do
sense a presence here.

141
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:27,520
I assume this youth is not dead.

142
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:33,997
This boy...

143
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:36,380
So, Mina and I are his parents.

144
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,100
Did he say boy?

145
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:43,620
As the captain says, this boy is our son.

146
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,624
Well, I am thoroughly confused.

147
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,877
Hold on, why isn't anyone
having much of a reaction?

148
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:52,517
I would assume a revelation like
this would elicit shouts of surprise.

149
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,430
What?

150
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:55,457
You're telling us you two are married?

151
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:57,217
That's what I was waiting for, Lamas.

152
00:07:57,300 --> 00:08:00,197
I could tell there was something
going on between them by the fighting,

153
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:03,045
but I had no clue they
were married with a kid.

154
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:05,997
Much less that their kid
was asleep inside a crystal.

155
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:08,897
It'd be much more unnatural
not to be surprised.

156
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:10,509
Sorry to keep it a secret.

157
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,505
It's been nearly 20 years
since we got married.

158
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,780
Yes, my love. That it has.

159
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:19,657
We might as well share that Aka
and Shiro are our sons, too.

160
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:20,570
What?

161
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,920
I'm surprised you never caught on.

162
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:24,334
Sorry for the secrets.

163
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:28,160
It makes sense.

164
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,897
Aka and Shiro's presence
always seemed similar

165
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:33,333
to the captains and vice-captains to me.

166
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:34,977
What, not surprised, Evie?

167
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:37,897
I've never seen you lose your
cool, and to be perfectly frank,

168
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:39,717
I was kind of looking forward to it.

169
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:42,297
I'm sorry to betray your
expectations, Captain,

170
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:45,321
but I've had a vague notion
of it for a while now.

171
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,897
Man, you really are a
cunning one, aren't you?

172
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:51,657
So I guess all this means that you two
are that boy's big brothers then, right?

173
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:52,570
Not quite.

174
00:08:52,653 --> 00:08:54,057
He's actually the oldest.

175
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:56,258
Yep, matter of fact, we're triplets.

176
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,330
What?

177
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:58,780
That's not all.

178
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,157
Before we reveal our wishes to you all,

179
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:04,711
we should explain the situation
with our sleeping son here.

180
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:08,997
You and me, I bet you already
know what this crystal is.

181
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:11,977
Well, it seems like it's
some form of crystal coffin.

182
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:12,890
Correct.

183
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:14,020
As I expected.

184
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:15,540
I'm not following.

185
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:19,497
It's an old magic item, though
ancient might be an even better word.

186
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:22,737
When you're inside one, a
person becomes frozen in time,

187
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:25,349
with all their biological
processes halted.

188
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:27,277
He's in there for a reason.

189
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,948
He has a negative blessing.

190
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,820
A negative blessing?

191
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:33,700
As you know, blessings are superpowers.

192
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,647
They're bestowed upon
us by a benevolent god.

193
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:40,497
Lamas has the blessing of might,
and I guess Boxo has his barrier.

194
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,815
On the other hand, a negative
blessing is the opposite.

195
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:46,780
A worthless power bestowed
by a malevolent god.

196
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:50,791
Thanks to that, our son couldn't
even manage everyday life.

197
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:54,500
We couldn't bear to watch
him get worse by the day.

198
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:57,497
So we decided to let him
stay here, unconscious,

199
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:59,637
until we could find a way to help him.

200
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:04,357
So time has stood still for him, and he's
remained the same age all these years.

201
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:07,077
The other two triplets
didn't have any issues.

202
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:09,597
He alone ended up with
a negative blessing.

203
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:11,960
As for what that is...

204
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:14,800
The blessing of decay.

205
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:19,860
An utterly horrid blessing where
not only does anything he touch rot,

206
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,740
but his own body would
also gradually decay.

207
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:28,560
To make matters worse, he was born
with the blessing of hyper-recovery.

208
00:10:29,700 --> 00:10:33,220
He feels the pain of his
body continuously decaying,

209
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:36,400
all while it regenerates
due to hyper-recovery.

210
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:40,140
That vicious cycle will
continue until the day he dies.

211
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:42,760
How'd he get the negative blessing?

212
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:47,218
Once, a long time ago, we all but
wiped out a certain team of hunters.

213
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:48,557
And to get revenge,

214
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:53,522
they used an ancient cursed item to saddle
our poor family with this wretched fate.

215
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:54,790
But unfortunately,

216
00:10:54,873 --> 00:10:57,437
it took me longer than
I cared to admit to even

217
00:10:57,520 --> 00:11:00,755
realize he'd been given the
horrible blessing of decay.

218
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:06,044
By the time I figured it out, he could
hardly even get around because of the pain.

219
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:07,615
Great parenting, huh?

220
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,579
After hearing all this, it's clear.

221
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:13,527
Even an idiot could
guess what their wish is.

222
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:18,277
In case it's not obvious, our wish is
to get rid of his negative blessing.

223
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:21,184
We're prepared to do
anything to make it happen.

224
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:25,217
This crystal coffin's likely to be
effective for another year to two at most.

225
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:26,320
Maybe even less.

226
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:29,340
We don't have much time.

227
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:31,999
Now, for what we wanted to discuss.

228
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:35,940
Would you defect with us
to the Netherlord's side?

229
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,030
Foxo!

230
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,940
Would you defect to the Netherlord's side?

231
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:48,020
But Captain, how could you?

232
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:50,217
He's the one who tried to
kill us, or did you forget?

233
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:53,337
I would happily sacrifice
every single one of your

234
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,977
lives if it meant my son
would no longer be in pain.

235
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:59,017
My family is the most important
thing in the world to me.

236
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:03,260
For the sake of argument, let's just
say that we did agree to defect.

237
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:05,420
How would we even go about it?

238
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:09,297
The commander who was on this stratum
seems to be willing to arrange it.

239
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:14,262
She was already planning on contacting us,
actually, under the Netherlord's orders.

240
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:15,680
You don't say.

241
00:12:16,180 --> 00:12:19,897
The four of us want to conquer the
strata and have our wish granted.

242
00:12:19,980 --> 00:12:21,957
The Netherlord wants us to
get through to the final

243
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:24,877
stratum so we can take full
control over the dungeon.

244
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,980
Our interests happen to coincide.

245
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:29,437
You really think he'll honor
his side of the bargain?

246
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:30,800
You know who he is.

247
00:12:30,940 --> 00:12:32,797
Yes, I know full well who he is.

248
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,920
But be realistic.

249
00:12:34,060 --> 00:12:37,937
How long would it take for us to defeat him
and get the dungeon back to what it was?

250
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:41,017
We don't have near enough
time to do this the slow way.

251
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:45,924
Even if we know we're walking into a trap,
it's the only hope we have to cling to!

252
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,380
So I'll ask again.

253
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:51,877
Aren't there any of you who'd be
willing to defect along with us?

254
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:56,078
We know the situation now, but our
answer to that question is obvious.

255
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:57,792
So much for negotiation.

256
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:00,600
Well, that's too bad. You're Ekpa.

257
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:01,840
Too bad.

258
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:04,988
Boxxo, you're the one
we wanted most of all.

259
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,419
Boxxo stays with me no matter what.

260
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,482
I won't hand him over to anyone.

261
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:14,366
Part of a clergyman's duty is to lead
allies from Fali back to a righteous path.

262
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:18,337
Perhaps a little tap from my weapons
will knock you all back to your senses.

263
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:19,360
Or kill us.

264
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:22,497
It's not like we're planning
to go around killing anyone.

265
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:26,197
All we're going to do is use the
Netherlord so we can conquer the dungeon.

266
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:28,957
He's likely thinking something
along those same lines.

267
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:31,837
And he'll throw you to the
wolves once he's done with you.

268
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:32,750
Now what?

269
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:35,697
Blamas doesn't have full control
over her blessing and might.

270
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:38,777
It's too dangerous for her to
fight them under those conditions.

271
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:39,690
I know.

272
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,780
Thanks for the save, Boxxo.

273
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:50,257
Wait a minute, is this supposed to be me?

274
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:52,097
There's gotta be a better option.

275
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:53,160
Sa-o-bi.

276
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:56,697
I'll have to think of a
more appropriate nickname.

277
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:59,977
I'm sad to say it looks like
there's no avoiding a fight.

278
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:01,884
All right, let's do this, boys.

279
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:03,728
Heard loud and clear, Pops.

280
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:08,737
Didn't know you excelled
in post-combat, too.

281
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:10,780
Good enough, but barely.

282
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,300
Hey, I'm here too.

283
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:18,917
That's terrifying.

284
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,277
One hit would be lethal.

285
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,277
Don't worry, Akka.

286
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:24,497
If you die, I'll take care of the ladies
you were planning to hook up with.

287
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:27,580
I didn't want to fight,
but you're forcing my hand.

288
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:31,257
I want to jump in too, but the room's
so small, I'd hit my own people.

289
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:34,857
I guess I'll just have to count on
Mishel and Heavy to do the heavy lifting.

290
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:35,900
No pun intended.

291
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:40,037
Don't tell me you're
slowing down already, Heavy.

292
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:42,649
I didn't expect your
blades to be poisoned.

293
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:44,857
Hey, now, the poison won't kill you.

294
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:47,469
It'll just make you
hurt real bad all over.

295
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:48,790
Hold on.

296
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:50,257
Why isn't it hurting you?

297
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:53,277
Oh, well, that would be
because I'm using my blessing.

298
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:55,242
It can temporarily relieve pain.

299
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:57,617
You have a blessing that can relieve pain?

300
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:58,530
Yes.

301
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:01,337
Neither the illusions nor
mind meddling are magic.

302
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:03,557
They're my blessing of
sensory manipulation.

303
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:06,220
I've never heard of a blessing like that.

304
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:07,880
Oh, Hulemy.

305
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,477
Methinks you might have
heard of my blessing.

306
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:11,390
Yeah.

307
00:15:11,473 --> 00:15:14,717
As far as blessings go, it's
about as rare as Boxo's Barrier.

308
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,577
Are you cool with me explaining it?

309
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:17,490
Indeed.

310
00:15:17,573 --> 00:15:18,517
I would not object there.

311
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:22,137
This very rare blessing allows
you to control a person's senses,

312
00:15:22,220 --> 00:15:24,877
to manipulate their sight,
hearing, smell, and taste,?

313
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:27,666
and potentially control
the sensation of pain.

314
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:29,050
Wait a minute!

315
00:15:29,133 --> 00:15:31,057
Are you saying it could
get rid of my son's pain?

316
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:32,560
Unfortunately, no.

317
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:35,880
I cannot use its analgesic
effect on other people.

318
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:37,840
We'll dagnab it.

319
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:39,460
I do apologize.

320
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,351
I hate to disappoint you.

321
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:45,897
Fighting against you is such a bummer!

322
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:48,397
Can't you, like, hold back even
just a little and let you get away?

323
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:51,440
I think not. Wilmena! Aka! Shiro! Yay!

324
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,600
Here we go! What's this?

325
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:55,642
Are they about to try something?

326
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:02,437
What's going on he was fine
just a moment ago heavy

327
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:05,897
i don't know what he did
to heavy But whatever they

328
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:09,397
try i'll repel it with my
barrier heavy's not the

329
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:12,715
only one in this Fight who's
been hiding what he can do

330
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,320
But i didn't turn it off

331
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:25,297
This is the same spell filmina used in
the battle against the crocodile fiends I

332
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:30,145
never thought I'd have to use the secret
weapon I was saving for the Nether Lord.

333
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,080
Master Botso! Comrades!

334
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,297
I will give chase immediately!

335
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:37,210
No, don't!

336
00:16:37,293 --> 00:16:41,217
We don't know what the captain's power
does, so going after him is too risky.

337
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:43,020
We should see to Heavy first.

338
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,700
Alas, they really fooled us, eh?

339
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:48,597
I suppose the man's not
our captain for nothing.

340
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:50,617
How can you be so calm about this?

341
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:52,577
Were you putting on an
act to help them get away?

342
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:54,500
No, and perish the thought.

343
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:57,657
Severe pain had me waylaid
till mere moments ago.

344
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:59,217
Even right now, as we speak,

345
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:02,357
I am once again using my blessing
to relieve the waves of agony.

346
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:06,417
His blessing halted your blessing
and neutralized Boxo's barrier, too?

347
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:09,137
Also, the captain's eyes
were glowing red back there.

348
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:10,397
Yeah, that was creepy.

349
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:11,715
They were bright red.

350
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,080
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

351
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:17,320
From that data, my guess is that
it's the blessing of eye breach.

352
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:21,357
It's practically a legend, but it
lets you negate other blessings.

353
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:24,297
The captain's blessing of eye
breach means serious trouble for me.

354
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:26,792
If I can't use my barrier or telekinesis,

355
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:29,567
I'm nothing but a
convenient vending machine.

356
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:30,880
Oh, right.

357
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:33,017
That's still a useful
thing to be, I guess.

358
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:35,957
We need to report this to
the director immediately.

359
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:38,597
Shall we return to the
village and seek him out?

360
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:40,340
Yeah, we had better do that.

361
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:44,277
They just ran off and didn't think
twice about leaving their son behind.

362
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:47,277
They must know we would
never harm the poor child.

363
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:49,480
He has done nothing wrong after all.

364
00:17:56,160 --> 00:18:00,807
To get right to the point, I added Kerry
Oil and the others to the wanted list.

365
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:06,641
To think that our comrades would betray us,
it would appear I have been quite naive.

366
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:07,950
Sorry.

367
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:10,017
I wish they would have
told us about it from

368
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:12,437
the start before making this awful choice.

369
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:15,637
The Vice-Captain's temperament
probably had something to do with it.

370
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,800
She isn't good at asking for help.

371
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:20,537
I still wish they would
have just talked to us.

372
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:21,940
Yes, me too.

373
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:25,137
The way they left their
precious son behind,

374
00:18:25,220 --> 00:18:29,097
that might be our fool captain's
way of sending a cryptic message.

375
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:31,886
If only they hadn't felt
backed into a corner.

376
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:35,437
I should probably feel angry that
they've done something so treacherous,

377
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:36,477
but I don't know.

378
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:38,420
I just can't bring myself to.

379
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:42,220
Yes, well, if we can
believe what Kerry Oil said,

380
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:44,517
they'll likely go to the final stratum and

381
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:46,817
begin their foolish attempt to conquer it.

382
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:47,730
One question.

383
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:50,537
How do you suppose they mean
to travel between strata?

384
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:52,200
I had that same thought.

385
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:56,677
The Netherlord might have some magic item
that allows for movement between strata.

386
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:58,957
Or they could be planning
to defeat the Stratum

387
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:01,417
Lords and use the transfer
circles from that.

388
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:02,330
Oh, right.

389
00:19:02,413 --> 00:19:04,817
There's a Stratum Lord in
the depths of each stratum.

390
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,606
A transfer circle appears
when you defeat one.

391
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:08,677
At the same time,

392
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:12,477
I don't think we really need to worry that
they'll conquer the dungeon anytime soon.

393
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:13,660
What do you mean?

394
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:17,077
That the four of them are not
nearly powerful enough on their own.

395
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:20,017
If they truly mean to
outmaneuver the Netherlord,

396
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:22,637
they'll need to enlist
some trustworthy comrades.

397
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:27,557
Which means they'll likely try to win over
someone new or recruit old acquaintances.

398
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:29,980
Oh, the other two menagerie folks.

399
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:32,554
Ah, yes, talk about a pair of oddballs.

400
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:35,017
If the captain can manage
to cajole or bribe them,

401
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:37,797
I can very well see them
coming to his family's aid.

402
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,500
Uh, I wouldn't rule that out.

403
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:45,257
Damn, if Heavy's calling them oddballs,
then those two have got to be super weird.

404
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:47,717
With that in mind, I think
we should update our plan.

405
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:50,037
While we're attempting to restore
the peace on each stratum,

406
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:52,197
we should also attempt
to make contact with the

407
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:55,097
remaining members and win
them over to our side.

408
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:56,356
Excellent, Director.

409
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:59,557
However, while I know those two can
be found somewhere in the dungeon,

410
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:02,477
I have no notion of which
stratum they might be on.

411
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:05,417
It was once my duty to locate
them for the menagerie,

412
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:08,197
but that was before my
unfortunate imprisonment.

413
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:12,377
In the middle of an important mission,
he was detained for acts of perversion.

414
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:14,077
Back to more pressing matters.

415
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:17,617
We're in a bit of a bind now since we
can't travel freely between strata.

416
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:20,977
Then I think we should return
to the Clearflow Lake Stratum.

417
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:22,837
Restoration has only just begun.

418
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,957
There's a long list of things to do.

419
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,040
Yeah, he's right.

420
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:29,516
Time to head back to Clearflow
Lake Stratum, everyone.

421
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:33,566
So many intense things
happen on this stratum.

422
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:37,439
It's sure been a crazy time
to be a vending machine.

423
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:42,897
Here I am, doing something as important as
crushing the Netherlord's evil ambitions.

424
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:46,157
That would make sense if I were in
the role of some legendary hero,

425
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:48,880
but, like, I'm a vending machine.

426
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:53,257
Nevertheless, while my body might be
inorganic, my heart is still human.

427
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:54,752
I want to save everyone.

428
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:57,877
A lot has happened, but let's
fight on together, Boxo.

429
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:58,790
Hello there.

430
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:02,477
Well, I don't know how much I
can manage as a vending machine,

431
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:07,148
but I do know I'll devote all my electricity
to keeping Lamas and me together.

432
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:11,100
All right, I'm activating it now.

433
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:14,057
Has it been tampered with?

434
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:14,970
What's going on?

435
00:21:15,053 --> 00:21:16,897
Everyone, evacuate the transfer circle.

436
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:19,333
Yeah, I would, except I can't even move.

437
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:20,260
Mokso! Mokso!

438
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:25,790
Huh?

439
00:21:25,873 --> 00:21:26,703
Where am I?

440
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:28,700
This isn't good.

441
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:32,117
Did I get sent to some
other stratum by myself?

442
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:34,077
Based on what Hulemy was shouting,

443
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:37,117
something must have gone wrong
with the transfer circle.

444
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:40,800
I hope everyone's okay, and
I'm worried about llamas.

445
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:45,959
Oh, I'd better move, or I'll be in
the way if someone else transfers.

446
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:51,640
Okay, so now what?

447
00:21:51,900 --> 00:21:54,517
Should I find a way to
open the door and go out?

448
00:21:54,600 --> 00:21:56,540
Or wait here and see who comes?

449
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:03,360
Hulemy, Director Bear, Llamas, huh?

450
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:04,740
Where's Llamas?

451
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:25,637
I don't know what I'm saying to you,

452
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:32,317
but I don't know what

453
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:36,260
I'm saying to you.

454
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:41,157
I'm going to take a step and take a step.

455
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:44,297
I'm going to walk you through.

456
00:22:44,380 --> 00:22:45,537
I'm going to take a step.

457
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:48,380
I'm going to take a step.

458
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:50,746
I'm going to change tomorrow!

459
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:56,577
This melody?

460
00:22:56,660 --> 00:22:58,366
I'm going to go over the way.

461
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:00,197
I'm going to move on.

462
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:02,057
I'm going to move on.

463
00:23:02,140 --> 00:23:03,980
I'm going to be the only one.

464
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:15,317
See you

465
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:20,020
next time.

466
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:36,700
You could even win a reward.

467
00:23:37,740 --> 00:23:39,858
I look forward to serving you again.
